# Demo frontend env template — demo.app-juli.com (apps/demo)
#
# Copy to ~/Juli-AI-v2/apps/demo/.env.production on the VPS if needed.
# NEVER commit real values. Mock mode itself requires no backend credentials
# or API URL — no NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL, DATABASE_URL, or TikTok secrets are
# required at build or runtime.
#
# THE GOOGLE SIGN-IN DOOR IS THE EXCEPTION (issue #1905). Next.js inlines
# NEXT_PUBLIC_* variables at `next build` TIME, never at runtime — a value
# added here on the server, or to a systemd EnvironmentFile, changes nothing
# already built. Both variables below must be present when the release
# workflow's `app-release-artifact` job (matrix.app == 'demo') runs
# `next build`, sourced from the two repository secrets
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY — never as a
# literal in the workflow, never committed here. Names only, below:

# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Optional public app URL (informational; not required for mock mode).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL=https://demo.app-juli.com
